From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dhtmled: the DHTML Editing Control edits a live MSHTML document (9601)

On Windows the control (and its page-safe twin DHTMLSafe) edits a real
MSHTML document in design mode: DocumentComplete fires when MSHTML has
loaded it, DOM is that document, the DECMD_ commands of ExecCommand and
QueryStatus are MSHTML's editing commands, and DocumentHTML/IsDirty follow
the edits. Here the control only kept the source text, and ExecCommand,
QueryStatus, SetContextMenu and PrintDocument were E_NOTIMPL.

docsite.c hosts the document (client site, in-place site, frame, UI
handler, ready-state sink). Sited in a container the control activates the
document in place in the container's window (windowed, as an ATL control
does); ExecCommand/QueryStatus map DECMD_ to IDM_ (CGID_MSHTML) and the
OLECMDF state to DECMDF_; get/set commands pass their values; DOM gives
the live document; DocumentHTML, DocumentTitle, Save and the data object
take MSHTML's current source; IsDirty includes MSHTML's; Save clears it;
BrowseMode switches design mode; SetContextMenu takes script arrays or
SAFEARRAYs, and a right click fires ShowContextMenu, shows the program's
items and fires ContextMenuAction; PrintDocument is IDM_PRINT (with or
without the dialog); TranslateAccelerator goes to the document. DHTMLSafe
(registered by the type library but refused by DllGetClassObject) is the
same editor with IDHTMLSafe and _DHTMLSafeEvents. Without MSHTML (Gecko
missing) the control keeps its text-only behaviour.

Not done: the TriEdit table commands (DECMD_INSERTTABLE and the row,
column and cell commands) and the DEInsertTableParam /
DEGetBlockFmtNamesParam helper classes; LOCK_ELEMENT and the text-layer
z-order commands have no MSHTML command.
---
--- a/dlls/dhtmled.ocx/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/dhtmled.ocx/Makefile.in
@@ -4,5 +4,6 @@
